# Managed by btrfs-setup.sh (CST).
# Automatic block-group reclaim ("auto-balance") for the root btrfs filesystem,
# a last line of defence against ENOSPC rather than routine housekeeping:
#   dynamic_reclaim:  the reclaim threshold stays 0 until unallocated space
#                     (summed over devices) drops below ~10 data chunks
#                     (~10 GiB here); from there it rises towards 100%, so
#                     half-empty data block groups get compacted harder the
#                     closer the fs is to full;
#   periodic_reclaim: lets the cleaner thread run that check periodically.
# btrfs-health-check warns much earlier (50 GiB unallocated per device).
# Only data block groups: relocating metadata needs metadata space itself.
# `w-` keeps this harmless on kernels/rescue boots without these sysfs knobs.
w- /sys/fs/btrfs/@UUID@/allocation/data/dynamic_reclaim - - - - 1
w- /sys/fs/btrfs/@UUID@/allocation/data/periodic_reclaim - - - - 1
